                "index_texts": [
                    "Sing Sing (2023)\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\nSing\u00a0Sing\n\n\n        \n    \n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t Synopsis Trust the\u00a0process. Divine G, imprisoned at Sing Sing for a crime he didn\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t commit, finds purpose by acting in a theatre group alongside other incarcerated men in this story of resilience, humanity, and the transformative power of\u00a0art. \n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t Cast   \n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tPopular reviews\n\t\tMore\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t      every time \u00e2\u20ac\u0153as himself\u00e2\u20ac\ufffd rolled across the screen tears also rolled down my face. what a beautiful movie    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t      A very special movie. A reminder that in a broken system that only seeks to oppress, art serves not only as catharsis, but as liberation.    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t      nothing will radicalize you faster than knowing literally anything about the US prison system    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t      Clarence \u00e2\u20ac\u0153Divine Eye\u00e2\u20ac\ufffd Maclin performance of the year.    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t      Why does the caged bird sing? Because he has a voice. And the world deserves to hear it.    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t      \u00e2\u20ac\u0153as himself\u00e2\u20ac\ufffd \u00e2\u20ac\u0153as himself\u00e2\u20ac\ufffd \u00e2\u20ac\u0153as himself\u00e2\u20ac\ufffd ohhh the tears ohhhhhh the tears    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t      a tremendously tenderhearted tribute to the therapeutic power of the artistic process, overflowing with honesty and humanity in every single scene thanks to what is not only the ensemble of the year, but also one for the ages.    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t      THAT'S RIGHT BABY THEATRE IS FUCKING LIFE CHANGING I WILL SCREAM IT TO THE ROOFTOPS IF I HAVE TO WOOOOO I LOVE THEATRE    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t      shawshank redemption but for the theatre kids    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t      just being real with each other and vulnerable. it\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s something men don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t really get to do too often.    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t      \u00e2\u20ac\u0153Freddy in this?\u00e2\u20ac\ufffd \u00e2\u20ac\u0153Freddy is definitely in this.\u00e2\u20ac\ufffdI understand why this is the case, but it bums me out that the conversation around how emotional movies like this never talk about how funny or charming they are. Like that\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s what really made me love this movie. At one point I turned to my friend and joked \u00e2\u20ac\u0153this shit makes me wanna go prison\u00e2\u20ac\ufffd but I did kind of mean it! The cast of characters we meet here are such lovely, full people, and I could\u00e2\u20ac\u2122ve lived here for much longer. I had a happy cry to the scene when they\u00e2\u20ac\u2122re all dancing. Also loved seeing the actual play! Clarence Maclin should\u00e2\u20ac\u2122ve been in Oscar conversations! Colman Domingo remains That Guy and it\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s his Oscar to lose imo.   \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t      all aboard the colman domingo should win an oscar for this movie train.\u00e2\u2022\u00ad\u00e2\u201d\ufffd\u00e2\u201d\ufffd\u00e2\u201d\ufffd\u00e2\u201d\ufffd\u00e2\u201d\ufffd\u00e2\u201d\ufffd\u00e2\u201d\ufffd\u00e2\u201d\ufffd\u00e2\u201d\ufffd\u00e2\u201d\ufffd\u00e2\u2022\u00b0\u00e2\u2022\u00ae\u00e2\u201d\ufffd\u00e2\u201d\u00b3\u00e2\u201d\u00b3\u00e2\u201d\u00b3\u00e2\u201d\u201c\u00e2\u201d\ufffd\u00e2\u201d\u00b3\u00e2\u201d\u00b3\u00e2\u201d\u00b3\u00e2\u201d\u00b3\u00e2\u201d\u201c\u00e2\u201d\ufffd\u00e2\u201d\u00bb\u00e2\u2022\u2039\u00e2\u2022\u2039\u00e2\u201d\u00bb\u00e2\u201d\u00bb\u00e2\u201d\u00ab\u00e2\u201d\u00a3\u00e2\u201d\u00bb\u00e2\u2022\u2039\u00e2\u2022\u2039\u00e2\u201d\u00bb\u00e2\u201d\u00ab\u00e2\u201d\u2014\u00e2\u201c\u017e\u00e2\u201d\u00bb\u00e2\u201d\u00bb\u00e2\u201d\ufffd\u00e2\u201c\u017e\u00e2\u201d\u00bb\u00e2\u201d\u00bb\u00e2\u201c\u017e\u00e2\u201d\u